================================================================================
Third-party material contained in dist/
================================================================================

These are compiled into `dist/plantuml-engine.js` and `dist/plantuml-engine.cjs`.
Each came to this project through PlantUML, which ships the same material.

ASCIIMathML (as ASCIIMathTeXImg)
    License:  MIT
    Copyright (c) Peter Jipsen (ASCIIMathML 1.4.7, 2005)
              (c) David Lippman (TeX conversion, 2006)

    src/core/math/ASCIIMathTeXImg.ts and ASCIIMathTeXImgSymbols.ts translate
    PlantUML's ASCIIMathTeXImg.java, itself a port of ASCIIMathTeXImg.js. They
    convert <math> and @startmath notation to LaTeX.

Open Iconic
    License:  MIT
    Copyright (c) 2014 Waybury
    Source:   https://github.com/iconic/open-iconic (ICON-LICENSE)

    The glyph outlines behind <&name> creole and the openiconic pages
    (src/core/openiconic-glyphs-data.ts).

PlantUML themes
    Source:   PlantUML's src/main/resources/themes/, embedded verbatim in
              src/core/themes-source.ts

    All 44 themes are included. Each states its own author and license in
    its header, which is kept. By that header:
    - MIT: 31 themes, by Brett Schwarz (22), Drakemor (8) and KingPlus-lang
      (spacelab-white).
    - Apache License 2.0: mars, toy and vibrant, by future-architect
      (https://github.com/future-architect/puml-themes).
    - GPL 3+: sunlust, by Artem V. Ageev.
    - No license stated: amiga, blueprint, crt-amber, crt-green, mimeograph
      and plain (Matthew Leather), mono (Denis Bondarenko with Matthew
      Leather), carbon-gray (Bharat Rajagopalan) and _none_ (The-Lum, an
      intentionally empty theme).

